+/*
+ * x-lfs-known (POMPPC tcg/0051, docs/tcg-g4.md section 40): lfs as a
+ * producer of x-fp-known.  The same guest load (memop, mmu_idx, fault at the
+ * same place); then INDEX_op_ppc_fp32 with FPI_LFS takes the word (frA,
+ * zero-extended; frB, frC and the FPSCR input are the same temp, unused; nf
+ * is dead): a float32 zero or normal is converted by the host (vcvtss2sd,
+ * fcvt d, s: exact for these), anything else goes out of line to DOUBLE()
+ * of the ISA, which leaves the TB after the lfs when FPK_R was or'ed into
+ * the selector by a consumer (lfsk_slow_path()).  frT then holds fpi_zon()
+ * whenever the rest of the TB runs: it enters fpk_valid, this op its
+ * producer.  The update form writes rA before the op, so that the TB exit
+ * finds it done (the op syncs the globals; nothing can fault after the
+ * load).  The instruction is handled: fpk_scan() would drop everything at
